Menu="NetworkServices"
Title="Pangolin CLI"
Icon="pangolin_cli.png"
Markdown="false"
Cond="!file_exists('/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/pangolin_newt/PangolinNewtTab.page')"
---
<?
/* Pangolin CLI - standalone Settings entry.
 *
 * Shown only when the Pangolin Newt plugin is NOT installed. When it is, this
 * entry disappears and PangolinCLITab.page renders the same form as a tab
 * inside the shared "Pangolin" group, so the two plugins take one slot in
 * Settings instead of two. Both are thin wrappers around include/settings.php.
 *
 * The Cond above deliberately tests for Newt's *tab* page rather than just its
 * plugin directory: an older Newt plugin without grouping support has no such
 * file, so both plugins keep their own entry instead of forming a half-empty
 * group.
 *
 * Why the eval below instead of a plain include: Unraid renders a page by
 * running Markdown() over the raw .page text and only then eval'ing the
 * result (see generateContent() in DefaultPageLayout/MainContent.php). An
 * include would skip the Markdown step and the form's definition-list layout
 * would come out as literal text, so the two steps are reproduced here in the
 * same order, on the shared body. Markdown="false" above stops this wrapper
 * itself from being processed twice. Kept inline rather than wrapped in a
 * function so the body still evaluates in the page scope it expects.
 */
$docroot ??= ($_SERVER['DOCUMENT_ROOT'] ?: '/usr/local/emhttp');
$evalFile    = "$docroot/plugins/pangolin_cli/include/settings.php";
$evalContent = '?>'.Markdown(parse_text(file_get_contents($evalFile)));
include "$docroot/webGui/include/DefaultPageLayout/evalContent.php";
